Cyber Security Consultant

Division: Cyber & Information Security

Role: Cyber Security Consultant

Region: Europe

Country: United Kingdom

Pay: £45,000 per annum

Overview:

The Cyber & Information Security Division at Bradburys Group is currently recruiting a Cyber Security Consultant responsible for assessing the security posture of our clients’ systems, networks and infrastructure and providing recommendations to enhance their cyber security defences. You will work closely with clients to understand their specific security requirements, conduct assessments and develop customised cyber security solutions to address specific needs.

Responsibilities:

Following an induction, on-boarding and training schedule, you will be required to:

• Conduct risk assessments and audits of clients’ systems, networks, and applications to identify vulnerabilities and weaknesses

• Analyse security risks and threats and develop mitigation strategies and action plans to address identified issues

• Design and implement security controls, policies and procedures to protect against unauthorised access, data breaches, and other cyber threats

• Provide guidance and recommendations on best practices, compliance requirements, and industry standards (e.g., ISO 27001, NIST, GDPR)

• Assist clients in incident response and remediation efforts in the event of a security breach or cyber attack

• Collaborate with clients’ IT teams and stakeholders to ensure the successful implementation and maintenance of cyber security measures

• Stay updated on emerging threats, trends and technologies within the field and provide thought leadership and expertise to clients and internal teams

• Demonstrate highest standards of customer-facing skills and customer care

Essential requirements:

• A five-year checkable work history

• Proof of Right to work in the UK

• Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology or related field (Master’s degree preferred)

• Professional certifications in cyber security such as CISSP, CISM, CEH, or similar

• Proven experience in cyber security consulting and experience in assessing, designing, and implementing cybersecurity solutions

• Deep understanding of cyber security principles, practices, technologies and methodologies

• Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to assess complex security issues and develop effective solutions

• Excellent communication and interpersonal skills with the ability to effectively communicate technical concepts to non-technical stakeholders

• Ability to work independently and as part of a team, managing multiple projects and priorities effectively

• Proficiency in cyber security tools and technologies, as well as industry standards and regulatory requirements

• An excellent command of English communication skills (written, oral, email)

• Ability to adapt at all times

• Excellent time-keeping/time management

• Full UK Driving licence

Core hours:

• Full-time

Disability Confident Employer

Bradburys Group is a Disability Confident Employer, committed to building an inclusive and accessible workforce. We actively encourage applications from individuals with disabilities and long-term health conditions. Applicants who declare a disability and meet the minimum essential criteria for the role will be guaranteed an interview, in line with our commitments under the Disability Confident scheme. All candidates are assessed based on merit, capability, and alignment with our operational values. We are committed to removing barriers to employment and will provide reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process and during employment, wherever reasonably practicable.

Armed Forces Commitment

We are recognised by the UK Ministry of Defence under the Defence Employer Recognition Scheme (ERS), having achieved Silver Award status in 2017. We actively encourage applications from service leavers, veterans, reservists, and military families. Applicants from the Armed Forces community who meet the minimum essential criteria for the role will be guaranteed an interview. We recognise the highly transferable skills, leadership, and operational discipline developed through military service and are committed to supporting a successful transition into civilian careers within the security and risk management sector.

