 Position Details

 • 
 Job Title
 Graphic Designer

 • 
 Number of Available Positions
 2

 • 
 Company
 CloudNet Technologies Limited

 • 
 Contract
 Permanent, full-time (37.5 hours per week)

 • 
 Salary (Depending on Experience)
 £34,000 to £36,000 per annum

 • 
 Location
 Unit 8B, Redfern Industrial Estate, Hyde SK14 1RD, United Kingdom

 Note
 Preference will be given to candidates from within the country. However, applicants from outside the UK are also welcome to apply.

 About the Role

 CloudNet Technologies Limited is expanding its professional graphic design and visual communication services in response to growing commercial demand from clients. We are seeking highly creative and detail-oriented Graphic Designers to support the delivery of client-facing design projects across branding, digital graphics, website assets, marketing materials and visual communication outputs.

 This is a full-time role suited to candidates with strong creative ability, technical design knowledge and the capacity to produce high-quality commercial design work to client briefs, brand standards and project deadlines.

 Key Responsibilities

 • Collaborate with clients and internal project teams to understand design objectives, brand requirements, budgets and delivery timescales.

 • Create professional designs for websites, logos, brochures, social media, digital campaigns and other marketing or visual communication materials.

 • Develop brand assets, visual identity materials and design layouts aligned with client specifications and commercial requirements.

 • Research design trends, review existing brand materials and propose creative improvements where appropriate.

 • Prepare sketches, concepts, colour schemes, layouts, mock-ups and production-ready artwork.

 • Revise and refine design work in response to client feedback and project requirements.

 • Prepare clear design specifications, artwork files and instructions for digital publication, print production or wider commercial use.

 • Coordinate with technical, web and platform teams where graphic assets are required for websites, digital products or client-facing business platforms.

 • Manage multiple design briefs simultaneously while maintaining high standards of accuracy, consistency and visual quality.

 Skills & Qualifications

 • Bachelor’s degree or equivalent qualification in Graphic Design, Visual Communication, Multimedia Design, Game Artistry or a closely related creative design discipline.

 • Demonstrable professional experience in graphic design, visual communication or related creative design work.

 • A strong portfolio evidencing relevant commercial design projects across digital and/or print media.

 • Proficiency in Adobe Creative Suite, including Photoshop, Illustrator and InDesign.

 • Familiarity with UI/UX design principles and digital user interface design.

 • Knowledge of branding, typography, colour theory, layout design and visual identity development.

 • Ability to prepare design concepts, mock-ups, artwork and production-ready materials.

 • Ability to manage multiple projects and client deadlines effectively.

 • Strong communication, collaboration, attention to detail and client liaison skills.

 Desirable

 • Experience in graphic design, multimedia design, digital media or a related creative industry.

 • Knowledge of animation, motion graphics or visual effects for digital media.

 • Experience using 3D tools such as Autodesk Maya or Blender.

 • Familiarity with game engines such as Unity or Unreal Engine.

 • Strong branding, colour theory and typography skills.

 Behaviours

 • A genuine passion for creative design, digital media and visual storytelling.

 • High personal standards and a strong, proactive work ethic.

 • A collaborative mindset with the ability to accept feedback and refine design work.

 • Commitment to equality, diversity and inclusion in the workplace.

 • Resilience, accountability and flexibility when adapting to changing project requirements.

 What We Offer

 • Competitive salary based on experience.

 • A broad range of commercial design projects across digital, branding and visual communication work.

 • Opportunities for professional development and career growth.

 • A collaborative, innovative and friendly working environment.

 How to Apply

 Please send your CV, cover letter and portfolio of recent projects to [email protected].

 Submit Your Application

 Join us and contribute to shaping impactful digital experiences!

 Diversity & Inclusion

 CloudNet Technologies Limited is a Disability Confident Committed Employer. We ensure our recruitment process is inclusive and accessible. We are committed to offering an interview to disabled people who meet the minimum criteria for the job, and we will anticipate and provide reasonable adjustments as required.

