#text-2266377532 {
 font-size: 1rem;
}

Assistant Commercial Manager + Commercial Manager – Transport & Infrastructure

Manchester Area, United Kingdom (Hybrid)

As a dynamic Assistant / Commercial Manager, this is a great opportunity to join CPC’s Transport and Infrastructure Division driving cost and contracts management across all areas of major transport and infrastructure projects.

Relevant skills and qualifications:

• Experience of working in a Quantity Surveying/ Commercial Management Team

• Experience of working Pre/ Post contract

• Experience supporting cost management activities including monthly reporting, cash flow control as well as forecasting of supported projects

• Awareness of the tendering and procurement process

• Stakeholder management experience

• Ability to work to tight deadlines and mandated processes with a high level of accuracy

• Strong understanding of Microsoft Office with a particular Excel

Ideally you will also have:

• Experience of working with NEC & NR forms of contract

• Experience working on complex, high profile projects

• Experience in a commercial environment within the transport and infrastructure environment

• Understanding of project and change management methods

• Degree qualification (or equivalent)

• Studying towards professional qualification (eg. RICS, CIPS, ICES) or desire to gain professional qualification

• Have a collaborative approach to both work and contract administration, able to work effectively on your own initiative and be a strong team player

• Ability to operate effectively within embedded delivery teams to drive the optimum commercial outputs in fast paced project delivery environments

How we will support you:

• Support and training towards gaining MRICS or equivalent qualifications, with a range of experts across the team and organisation to mentor you through your journey

• Regular 1-2-1s with your line manager and structured development objectives

• Buddy system to help integrate into the organisation

• Hybrid working (2/3 days per week between CPC offices and client site, and the remainder home working)

• Provide a supporting environment and positive culture to enable opportunities to progress within the Commercial Services division and build and develop your career

Manchester

