The opportunity

We’re looking for an experienced Project Manager to join our Transport & Infrastructure team in Manchester, delivering highways improvements, bus infrastructure, active travel and local authority transport schemes across the North West.

You’ll take ownership of projects from early development through to delivery, including business cases and funding applications, working with clients and multidisciplinary teams to turn transport priorities into successful, investable projects.

The work goes beyond infrastructure. You’ll help deliver schemes that improve connectivity, widen access to jobs and services, support sustainable travel and create safer, better-connected communities.

It’s an opportunity to broaden your experience, build strong client relationships and make a visible difference to the people and places our projects serve.

Big enough to deliver. Small enough to care.

CPC Project Services is an award-winning, independent Project Management and Cost Consultancy with more than 36 years’ experience across infrastructure, property and transformational change.

Since becoming employee-owned in 2024, our people have had a genuine stake in our success, creating a culture built on ownership, collaboration and pride.

With an ambition to reach £100m turnover by 2033, you’ll be joining an ambitious business where you can contribute to our future while developing your own career.

What you’ll be doing

You’ll provide proactive, commercially aware project leadership across the full delivery lifecycle.

• Establish project objectives, delivery strategies, programmes, budgets, governance and reporting

• Coordinate business cases, funding submissions and investment approvals, bringing together technical, financial and programme inputs

• Manage cost, programme, risk, change and quality

• Procure and manage consultants, contractors and multidisciplinary teams

• Lead project meetings and workshops, resolving issues and maintaining momentum

• Engage effectively with internal and external stakeholders, building strong relationships and maintaining clear, timely and consistent communication with clients, contractors, local authorities, funding bodies and delivery partners throughout the project lifecycle

• Support community and stakeholder engagement, ensuring local needs, social impact and wider benefits inform project development

• Provide clear reporting and advice to support effective decision-making

• Oversee projects through key stages from feasibility and design to procurement, construction and handover

• Support client engagement and the continued development of CPC’s North West Transport & Infrastructure business

What we’re looking for

• Project Management experience within transport or infrastructure sectors

• Ideally experience of highways, bus, active travel or local authority schemes

• Experience supporting business cases and funding applications

• Strong programme, cost, risk and stakeholder management skills

• Experience coordinating multidisciplinary teams

• Strong client relationship and communication skills, ideally within a local authority or public sector environment

• A proactive, collaborative and solutions-focused approach

• A relevant professional qualification or progress towards chartership would be advantageous

We’re looking for someone who combines strong project delivery with an understanding of the bigger picture – creating better connections, opportunities and outcomes for communities.

Why CPC?

Being employee-owned means our success is shared. You’ll have the opportunity to contribute ideas, influence how we work and benefit from the value we create together.

Alongside a competitive salary, we offer:

• Private healthcare for you and your family, including dental and optical

• Private pension scheme

• Hybrid and flexible working

• Travel insurance, including winter sports, for you, your partner and dependants

• Support with professional memberships, chartership and ongoing development

• Personal performance bonus

• Annual salary reviews

Build your career. Deliver projects. Make an impact.

If you want to deliver meaningful transport projects while building your career within an ambitious, employee-owned consultancy, we’d like to hear from you.

Apply to join CPC’s Transport & Infrastructure team in Manchester.

Diversity & Inclusion

CPC is an equal opportunities and Disability Confident employer. We welcome applications from all backgrounds and are committed to creating an inclusive environment where everyone can develop and succeed.

Recruitment agencies

We are not seeking external recruitment support for this position. Speculative CVs will not be considered.

Manchester

