 Senior Engineer

 Share

 Apply Now

 Company

 De Construction Solutions

 Location

 Piccadilly/Green Park, London

 Part-time/full-time

 Full-time

 Job Length

 Permanent

 Summary

 De Construction Solutions are looking to expand the team as we are currently supporting our clients with some technical challenging demolition and enabling works schemes. We are seeking candidates with Meng, MSc, BEng, or minimum equivalent in a Structural or Civil Engineering related degree).

The role is office-based with frequent site visits, inspections, and meetings in central London, and gives the right candidate a career path in the challenging yet rewarding construction engineering sector.

We offer full support in your CPD and training to further your professional learning.

We are part of the DE Group of companies, with close working relationships providing specialist engineering support to our sister companies, providing broad experience and networking to enable the right person to provide a first-class service.

Responsibilities — the successful applicant will provide engineering support to our clients working on technically challenging demolition and enabling works projects identifying and developing solutions with support from an experienced leadership team.

We are looking for candidates who can:

Technical understanding and application of engineering 

 • produce engineered solutions to construction problems at tender and project stages;

 • check and approve medium and low-risk engineered solutions produced by others;

 • provide guidance and coaching to Project Engineers/Junior Engineers and technicians;

 • be confident in the understanding and application of design codes and guidance;

 • provide technical support to identify and provide technically sound solutions to DE Group companies and external clients;

 • develop technical skills of junior staff.

Safety, Health, and Quality

 • ensure health and safety are key considerations in your engineered solutions;

 • ensure a designer's risk assessment/decision log has been completed and included as part of the design submission;

 • have and maintain an up-to-date CSCS card;

 • manage and deliver whole projects in line with the DE Group SHEQ processes and procedures and in line with ISO accreditations;

 • provide input into the continued betterment of integrated management systems.

Management and leadership

 • ensure the correct project administration and document management/record keeping is accurate and timely;

 • prepare and approve fee proposals for requested design briefs/scope of work items;

 • manage changes to our scope of work with the client, agreeing on actions and changes prior to implementing works;

 • perform your work in a professional manner and challenge yourself and others;

 • coordinate and manage the statutory, contractual, and commercial issues in relation to your projects;

 • take responsibility and full ownership for your work and that of others in your charge;

 • manage and lead resources across multiple projects.

Sustainability and the environment 

 • be considerate of the requirements for sustainability and the environment in your engineered solutions;

 • produce a positive impact with your designs considerate to waste, carbon, and resources.

Interpersonal skills and communication

 • communicate clearly and concisely with our client site teams both orally and in writing;

 • communicate ideas to technical and non-technical staff clearly and develop those skills in others;

 • input into the improvement of client relationships and business development;

 • input into industry best practices and working groups (e.g. TWF).

Qualifications — the candidate will ideally be Chartered with either the Institution of Structural Engineers or the Institution of Civil Engineers.

If you are interested in joining a dynamic company undertaking challenging projects, please, submit your CV. We look forward to hearing from you.

The DE Group is an equal opportunities employer.

**Mission of the role:**

We are looking for a Senior QA Engineer who automates by default, uses AI agents as everyday tools, and builds new ones where the off-the-shelf options fall short.

You will be part of one of our product squads, owning quality from requirements to release. At this level we also expect you to shape how the whole company tests: standards, tooling, and the shift from manual to automated testing.

Most of our systems today rely on manual tests. Manual testing stays part of the job, but your job is to make it the exception.

### Why work at Cobuilder?

- A key role in a growing international company
- The opportunity to influence the digitalization of the construction industry
- A highly skilled and engaged professional environment

### Main responsibilities include:

• Turn requirements into a test strategy, deciding for each scenario the right level: unit, integration, API, end-to-end or manual; 
• Build and maintain end-to-end and API test automation in Playwright, preferably with C# (TypeScript is also an option), and set up the CI/CD pipelines that run it automatically on every pull request, nightly and before each release; 
• Review the unit and integration tests our developers write in C#/.NET, as well as existing end-to-end suites, and recommend what to test where; 
• Use AI coding assistants and agents to generate, run and maintain tests, and build our own agents and automations where they add value; 
• Test manually where automation does not exist yet, and plan how to automate it; 
• Plan and run functional, API, and performance and load testing of complex web applications; 
• Maintain test plans and test cases in Azure DevOps Test Plans; 
• Report test results and quality risks clearly to engineers, product managers and business stakeholders; 
• Define testing and automation practices across squads and help developers and other QA engineers adopt them.

### What we are looking for:

• 5+ years in software QA, including 3+ years of hands-on test automation for web applications; 
• Strong Playwright skills with C# (preferred) or TypeScript; you write test code that others can maintain; 
• Ability to read C#/.NET code and judge whether unit and integration tests cover the right things; 
• A clear view of the test pyramid and when each level of testing pays off; 
• Experience testing REST APIs and running performance or load tests (for example k6, JMeter or Azure Load Testing); 
• Hands-on experience setting up and maintaining CI/CD pipelines (YAML) that run automated tests, including environments, test data, parallel runs and results reporting; 
• Daily, hands-on use of AI coding assistants or agents in your testing work, with examples you can show us; 
• An automation-first mindset, while still being thorough when testing manually; 
• Fluent English, written and spoken.

### Nice to have:

• You have built LLM-based automation tools yourself, for example Claude skills or plugins that use Playwright MCP server; 
• Experience with Azure DevOps Test Plans and CI/CD Pipelines; 
• Background in data or B2B SaaS products.

### Work-life at Cobuilder:

## Remote Work

For your productivity and effective team connections, we are offering a hybrid work approach. Sofia-based employees enjoy flexible weekly office collaborations (1 day per week/4 days monthly).

## Talent Development

For developing your talent, we offer various trainings and attendance at conferences.

## Flexible Working Hours

We offer flexible working hours and 23 days paid leave + 1 additional day after each year at Cobuilder (up to 26 days).

## Wellbeing

Additional health and dental insurance

## Referral bonuses

Up to 40% of our employees have been recommended by friends. We do love it when friends join the family!

## Social Activities

Expect a vibrant social calendar with celebrations, team-building events, and other activities.

### Hiring process:

We strive to be efficient, and we have 2 steps for hiring:

1. Technical interview:- Prepare a GitHub account, you will be invited to a private repository during the interview.

 – Prepare to share your screen, so if you have your own setup, feel free to use it. Make sure you can enable and disable your AI assistant.

2. Interview for background check and cultural fit

