• Optimise alerting thresholds, rules, and workflows to reduce noise and improve reliability.

• Contribute to the continuous improvement of monitoring practices, standards, and methodologies.

• Mentor junior developers and share best practices across the team.

Skills & Experience

• Proven hands-on experience with one or more monitoring and alerting tools (e.g., Dynatrace, AppDynamics, Datadog, Prometheus, Zabbix, Nagios, BigPanda, etc.).

• Strong programming/scripting ability (Python, PowerShell, JavaScript, or similar).

• Deep understanding of event management, log aggregation, and metrics pipelines.

• Familiarity with ITSM/ITIL practices and incident response workflows.

• Experience with cloud environments (AWS, Azure, GCP) and containerised applications (Docker, Kubernetes).

• Excellent problem-solving skills and the ability to translate business requirements into technical solutions.

• Strong communication skills with experience engaging enterprise-level customers.

Compensation

• Base Salary: £75,000 – £95,000 (depending on experience)

• Bonus: Performance-based, up to 10–15%

• Benefits: Competitive package with opportunities for learning, certification, and fast career progression in a start-up environment

What We Offer

