Insight Enterprises, Inc. is a Fortune 500 Solutions Integrator helping organizations accelerate transformation by unlocking the power of people and technology. We architect, build and manage solutions for complex IT environments to deliver outcomes that contribute to our clients' success.

&nbsp;

Our portfolio of digital transformation services includes deep expertise in cloud, data, AI, cybersecurity and intelligent edge. These services, augmented by Insight's longstanding relationships with 6,000+ technology partners across the globe, enable us to deliver the right technical solutions quickly and effectively. We're rated as a Great Place to Work, a Forbes Best Employer for Diversity and a Forbes World's Top Female-Friendly Company.

&nbsp;

About The Role&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Insight Enterprises is a Fortune 500 Solutions Integrator helping organisations accelerate transformation by unlocking the power of people and technology. Insight AI is the services arm delivering our AI, data and platform engineering work, and it holds Insight's global partnerships with Anthropic and OpenAI. &nbsp;
&nbsp;
The Partnership Solutions Consultant is Insight's specialist seller. You will own revenue for a service line and partner with Services Leadership, delivery teams and our Go-to-Market account executives to build and Execute client growth strategies, develop trusted executive relationships, shaping proposals with delivery, and running the sales process from first contact to signature.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
This PSC role is the first commercial hire into our Frontier AI seed model in EMEA. You will be responsible for building and closing a pipeline of Anthropic- and OpenAI-based services engagements strategy, governed deployment, agentic solutions, and AI Centre of Excellence programmes. Focused on mid-market and enterprise clients across EMEA. &nbsp;&nbsp;

&nbsp;

You will work directly with partner sellers at Anthropic and OpenAI to co-sell, and with Insight AI's solution architects and consultants to scope what we sell. This is a hunter's role with a consultant's brief. You will open the conversation, you will lead it with the executive who owns the budget, and you will close it.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
What You'll Do&nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;

• Own the sales process end to end. Run discovery, qualification (we use MEDDPICC and Miller Heiman Strategic Selling as our backbone), proposal, commercial negotiation and close for Frontier AI services engagements. Manage your pipeline in CRM with accurate stage, close date and forecast category.&nbsp;

• Sell at C-suite level. Build and sustain trusted relationships with CEOs, CFOs, CIOs, CTOs, CDOs and Heads of AI. Translate frontier model capability into business outcomes those stakeholders will fund — cost, revenue, risk, speed.&nbsp;

• Open new markets. Generate your own pipeline through outbound, partner co-sell, events and the Insight client base. Lead Insight's entry into new EMEA geographies and verticals where we have no existing Frontier AI footprint.&nbsp;

• Co-sell with Anthropic and OpenAI. Build working relationships with partner account executives and partner managers. Source and progress joint opportunities, qualify inbound partner referrals, and represent Insight AI credibly in partner forecast and pipeline reviews.&nbsp;

• Shape the proposition with delivery. Work with Insight AI's solution architects, product consultants and delivery leads to scope, price and propose engagements that we can deliver profitably. Develop customised proposals, business cases and executive presentations.&nbsp;

• Partner with the wider Insight go-to-market. Work alongside Insight's account executives and SDR team to position Frontier AI services into existing Insight accounts, and act as the subject-matter seller they bring into their clients.&nbsp;

• Feed the market back. Stay current on the frontier AI market, competitor positioning and regulatory landscape (EU AI Act, DORA, sector regulators) and bring that intelligence into our proposition and pipeline reviews.&nbsp;

• Report. Provide regular, honest pipeline and forecast updates to management, including the gaps.&nbsp;
&nbsp;

What Success Looks Like&nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;

• First 90 days: Fluent in the Insight AI Frontier AI proposition and delivery model. Active working relationships with Anthropic and OpenAI partner sellers in your territory. A qualified pipeline building in CRM with first executive-level meetings held.&nbsp;

• First 6 months: First Frontier AI services engagement closed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• First 12 months: Delivered against a bookings target defined by the business net-new logos. Established Insight AI as a referable partner within Anthropic and OpenAI's EMEA field teams.&nbsp;
&nbsp;

Must Have&nbsp;
&nbsp;
What we're looking for:&nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;

• 7+ years of quota-carrying B2B sales, with a demonstrable record of closing complex consultative deals with executive stakeholders. You have personally run a deal from first conversation to signature with a C-level economic buyer and can walk us through how.&nbsp;

• Experience selling professional services, managed services or SaaS platforms into mid-market or enterprise clients. You understand how services are scoped, priced and delivered, and you can hold a credible conversation with a solution architect.&nbsp;

• A self-starter who builds their own pipeline. You have opened new territories, new verticals or new buyer personas without an existing book to lean on, and you can show the outcomes.&nbsp;

• Commercially sharp: you qualify hard, you understand margin, and you walk away from bad deals.&nbsp;

• AI-first in how you work. You already use frontier AI tools daily to research accounts, prepare for meetings, draft proposals and sharpen your thinking and you can show us how. You can explain, in plain language, what a large language model can and cannot do for a business today.&nbsp;

• Comfortable with ambiguity. This is a seed-stage team. The proposition, the process and the territory will evolve, and you will help shape them.&nbsp;
&nbsp;

Strong Preference&nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;

• Experience selling AI, data, cloud or platform engineering services.&nbsp;

• Experience co-selling with a hyperscaler, ISV or AI vendor's field team.&nbsp;

• Working knowledge of MEDDPICC and/or Miller Heiman Strategic Selling.&nbsp;

• Exposure to regulated industries (financial services, higher education, public sector) and the governance conversation that comes with deploying AI in them.&nbsp;

• A slight technical background: a prior pre-sales, consulting or engineering role, or a technical degree, is useful but not essential.&nbsp;

• Fluent English plus professional working fluency in at least one other major EMEA language — German, French, Dutch, Spanish, Italian or a Nordic language would be welcome.&nbsp;

• Hiring manager interview: deal walk-through. Bring one C-suite deal you ran end to end — including what you got wrong.&nbsp;

• Insight AI Leadership Panel interview: a 30-minute executive pitch of a Frontier AI proposition to a mock CIO/CFO panel, followed by Q&amp;A with Insight AI delivery leadership.&nbsp;
&nbsp;

Why Insight AI&nbsp;
&nbsp;
You will be selling frontier AI services with two of the most important partners in the market, backed by a Fortune 500 integrator, client base and delivery capability — but inside a small team where&nbsp;
&nbsp;
your work is visible and your judgement shapes the business. Insight is a Great Place to Work and offers a competitive benefits package across all EMEA locations.&nbsp;

Insight Enterprises, Inc. is a Fortune 500 Solutions Integrator helping organizations accelerate transformation by unlocking the power of people and technology. We architect, build and manage solutions for complex IT environments to deliver outcomes that contribute to our clients' success.

&nbsp;

Our portfolio of digital transformation services includes deep expertise in cloud, data, AI, cybersecurity and intelligent edge. These services, augmented by Insight's longstanding relationships with 6,000+ technology partners across the globe, enable us to deliver the right technical solutions quickly and effectively. We're rated as a Great Place to Work, a Forbes Best Employer for Diversity and a Forbes World's Top Female-Friendly Company.

&nbsp;

WE ARE AMDARIS&nbsp;

At Amdaris, we bring together exceptional talent to deliver custom software solutions and drive digital transformation. Our acquisition by Insight last year has only solidified our standing in the market to become the leading provider of software solutions and paving the way for an exciting growth trajectory with ambitious future goals in AI Consulting.

Our expertise spans software development, cloud computing, IT strategy, and digital innovation, helping businesses optimise their technology and achieve their strategic objectives. With cutting-edge projects and a dynamic team, there has never been a better time to join us and be part of our journey to shape the future of technology.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Key Responsibilities:&nbsp;

• You will lead the review of client applications and their technology and product strategy.

• You will monitor emerging technologies, including AI, GenAI and machine learning trends, assessing their relevance and potential application within client solutions and strategies, and provide recommendations on adoption and integration opportunities.

• You will produce detailed reports providing guidance on enhancements, best practice, and risk mitigation.&nbsp;

• Working directly with clients, you will interact with senior stakeholders to understand the business objectives and strategy; uncover and challenge technical requirements, technology approaches, methodology, security and tech stack decisions in line with business goals.&nbsp;

• You will review and interpret architectural approach, infrastructure and data flows; assessing advising on best practice SDLC methodology and ways of working.&nbsp;

• Investigation will include the review of architecture diagrams and technical documentation.&nbsp;

• You will maintain effective internal relationships with sales, technical, product and delivery colleagues.&nbsp;

• You will be confident in providing technical support during sales pitches and proposals and will help to identify and promote additional value add services.&nbsp;

SOLUTIONS ARCHITECT (APPS &amp; AI) REQUIREMENTS&nbsp;

• Experience in software, application, and/or enterprise architecture methods and approaches.

• Experience defining and improving architectures, and linking decisions to business objectives and technology strategy.

• Hands-on delivery of GenAI solutions (LLMs, prompt engineering, AI features).

• Experience building, deploying, and operating cloud solutions, including the operational impact of design choices.

• Ability to review client applications, architecture, documentation, data flows, technology stacks, and SDLC/Agile practices.

• Hands-on credibility across languages, APIs, data stores, and integration patterns sufficient to challenge technical decisions.

• Ability to identify and mitigate security, privacy, data, operational, and AI-specific risks.

• Experience engaging senior clients, challenging assumptions, and influencing technical and non-technical audiences.

• Ability to produce decision-ready architecture reports covering findings, risks, and recommendations.

• Experience supporting pitches and proposals, shaping credible solutions, and identifying additional client value.

LIFE AT AMDARIS&nbsp;

• Private Medical Cover ✨ Your health is a priority and we’ve got you covered!

• Work from Anywhere Policy (EMEA) 🌍Flexibility to work from wherever inspires you!&nbsp;

• Flexible and Hybrid working 🧑‍💻A balance between office days and home comfort.

• Competitive Employer Pension contributions 💼 We invest in your future, today.&nbsp;

• Cycle to work scheme, Electric car scheme, Gym discounts 🚴 and many more flexible benefits to use at your leisure

• Health &amp; Wellbeing app 🧘 Access mindfulness tools, positivity boosts, and wellness support anytime

• Monthly social and charitable events 💙 Build connections and give back while having fun.

• Beer on Tap!! 🍻Raise a glass to celebrate the wins.

Applied Research Engineer

 21 Oct

 Written by Ben Thomas

 Project INSIGIA Logo

 METALLURGY & PHYSICS
SHEFFIELD, UK (CITY CENTRE LAB & HYBRID)
£50,000 pa | INITIAL 15-MONTH FIXED TERM WITH INTENTION TO RENEW
Introduction
Counterfeiting in critical supply chains is a growing threat across high-consequence industries. Backed by recent deeptech seed funding, our initiative, Project INSIGNIA, aims to make the physical counterfeiting of critical components impossible. We do this by embedding micro-scale cryptographic signatures directly into the internal structure of 3D-printed metal parts.
We are a small, focused team looking for our next colleague: an Applied Research Engineer to serve as the practical engine of Project INSIGNIA. You will work directly with the founders, taking digital models and established project milestones and turning them into working physical reality. This means taking full ownership of laboratory execution, from designing experimental architectures to validating physical cryptographic states.

As an Applied Research Engineer on Project INSIGNIA, you will:
• Devise and build the experimental plans required to write and read physical cryptography in metal alloys.

• Work hands-on with materials characterisation, including metallographic sample preparation, optical microscopy, and coordinating external X-ray computed tomography (XCT) scans.

• Test and iterate on sensor setups for non-destructive evaluation (NDE), exploring techniques such as acoustic resonance, eddy current, or bespoke electrical interrogation rigs.

• Coordinate trials with national user facilities and academic partners to validate our cryptographic states.

• Own laboratory execution, maintaining rigorous standards of data integrity and laboratory safety while moving quickly.

You will thrive in this role if you:
• Possess a solid core craft with a degree or hands-on background in Metallurgy, Materials Science, Physics, or Electrical Engineering.

• Default to high agency and autonomy, thriving in an R&D environment where the path forward is not always pre-charted. When an experimental setup fails, you diagnose the fault, redesign the experiment, and try again.

• Value pragmatism over pure theory, preferring robust, reproducible physical data over endless modelling.

• Have practical familiarity with non-destructive testing sensors, microstructural characterisation, metal additive manufacturing and coding/scripting (eg. Python) for experimental data capture (all valuable, though not all required).

Working at Instruct3D
• Small team, high agency: No bureaucracy or management layers. You own your work from concept to physical test.

• Pragmatic flexibility: Core working hours built around getting hard technical work done in the lab, balanced with genuine respect for personal and family commitments outside work.

• Craft over hype: We care about physics, sound metallurgy, and building things that reliably work in the physical world.

Compensation & Benefits
We believe in transparent compensation, solid security, and treating team members properly.
• Salary: £50,000 per annum.

• Contract: 15-month fixed-term role for Project INSIGNIA, with the intention to transition into a permanent position subject to future funding and project milestones.

• Pension: 5% employer pension contribution on all earnings.

• Financial wellbeing: An annual one-to-one review meeting with an independent financial adviser, plus year-round access for any pension or planning queries.

• Healthcare: Comprehensive private medical insurance including full cancer cover, full outpatient cover, mental health & therapies.

• Annual leave: 28 days annual leave, plus UK bank holidays.

• Start date: Onboarding by January 2027 at the latest, accommodating standard industry notice periods.

• Right to work: You must currently hold the right to work in the UK. Due to the strict timelines of this grant, we are unable to offer visa sponsorship.

Why Sheffield?
Our lab and office space sits in Sheffield city centre. Sheffield consistently ranks among the most affordable and liveable technical hubs in the UK, offering an exceptional quality of life without the punishing living costs of London, Oxford, or Cambridge.
Commutes are typically measured in minutes rather than hours, the local housing market remains genuinely accessible, and the Peak District National Park is just 20 minutes from the lab bench. It is an ideal base to build both a career and a life outside work.
How to Apply
We keep our hiring process straightforward, personal, and respectful of your time. No automated applicant tracking systems, no psychometric quizzes, and no artificial take-home assignments.
Step 1: Drop us a note
Send an email to [email protected] with your CV in PDF format attached. In the body of your email, please answer three short questions:
• Why do you want to work at an early-stage deeptech startup?

• Describe the physical project, experiment, or hardware setup you have built that you are proudest of.

• What is your current notice period or earliest start date, and do you currently hold the right to work in the UK?

What to expect next:
• Stage 1 (30 minutes): An informal video chat with the founders to discuss background, project scope, and mutual fit.

• Stage 2 (60 to 90 minutes): A technical deep dive where you walk us through a previous technical challenge or experimental rig, discussing first-principles physics, trade-offs, and failure modes.

• Stage 3 (In-person): A visit to our Sheffield lab to meet the team, inspect the hardware, and ensure the environment suits you.

Not the right role for you, but interested in what we do? We keep our core team lean, but we are always keen to hear from skilled engineers and scientists. Send a brief note and CV to [email protected].

