 Overview
Job summary
Nuttall Bowser are a specialist bridge engineering consultancy start-up, heading into our fourth year of business, based in Bristol operating throughout the UK and beyond. We work across numerous sectors delivering bridge engineering services across all asset lifecycle stages from asset management through to detailed design for asset owners, contractors, property developers and consulting partners. We are renowned for the quality of service we provide and differentiate our client and employee experiences through embodying our values: ‘Agile, Anticipate, Enhance, & Together’. 
We are based in the Generator Building within the Finzels Reach area of central Bristol – situated in a harbourside setting with just a 5min walk to Cabot Circus and a 10min walk to the train station. The Generator Building is grade II listed structure modernly restored to celebrate its heritage features and history, providing an appropriate fit to our business capability and culture. 
We are entering an exciting growth phase and seeking a Principal Engineer to enable further growth and success. We hire talented people who seek a challenge, are naturally open-minded, who want to share a journey, grow technically and personally without limits. 
You will join a high performing environment which aims to inspire, nurture and reward our people. We recognise that our people are by far our most important asset and thus our philosophy is that we hire great people and empower and support them in achieving their goals.
Responsibilities 
• Act as team leader with responsbility for resource management, team development and securing work

• Act as technical lead for delivery of examinations, assessments and design works

• Act as line manager and develop junior staff members

• Lead teams, plan & manage project delivery and act as main client contact

• Act as project manager and/or project director to support project delivery

Minimum Requirements
• 8 years plus post graduate experience in bridges discipline

• Chartered with ICE or IStructE

• Extensive experience in the examination, assessment, repair & design of bridge assets and working knowledge of Eurocode, British & DMRB standards

• Extensive technical delivery experience including technical leadership, project management and client facing 

Preferred Requirements
• 9+ years plus post graduate experience in bridges discipline

• Extensive experience in detailed design of reinforced concrete and steel superstructures and substructure/foundation design

• Strong experience in non-linear buckling Finite Element Analysis (FEA)

• Work winning experience including fee proposals and tender authoring

Equal opportunities
We are an Equal Opportunities Employer – we believe in enhancing our employees to reach their full potential without prejudice with all business hire, training, and career progression based solely upon the needs of the individual and the business. 

